      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Superman\"] With apologies to Marlon Brando, Glenn Ford, and people who pronounce the word ‘Krypton’ wrong, this movie would be even stronger if you cut out the first 45 minutes entirely and started with the very first shot in Metropolis. That’s when the story really begins anyway. Even in 1978, everyone knew Superman’s origin — or at least enough to understand the rest of the movie. The thing Superman still has going for it, even as its cutting edge you-will-believe-a-man-can-fly effects age, is Christopher Reeve. Very few comic book movies feature one performance as good as his Clark Kent or his Superma",
